hing that is  built on top of it now it is of course  well understood that people in the  retail market people in the financial  market and also folks who have been  building in and around the bitcoin and  crypto industry understand this asset  they understand how it works and they  understand what the financial elements  of it are but one person that you  probably would not expect to really  understand it is politicians and what we  saw last week at the texas blockchain  summit was ted cruz standing on stage or  sitting on stage giving a talk about  bitcoin and he had very articulate take  nick carter went ahead and transcribed  the entire uh talk but what i wanted to  do is i want to call it a very specific  part at one point ted cruz said it's a  weird point a lot of the discussion  around bitcoin views bitcoin as a  consumer of energy a lot of the  criticism directed at it is the  consumption of energy the perspective  i'm suggesting is very much the reverse  which is a way to strengthen our energy  infrastructure and it also has one of  the most exciting things about crypto is  the ability to unlock stranded  renewables so there are a lot of places  on earth where the sun shines a lot and  the wind blows a lot but there aren't  any power lines and so it's not  economically feasible to use that energy  and the beauty of bitcoin mining is that  if you can connect to the internet you  can use that energy and derive value  from those renewables in a way that  would be impossible otherwise and i  think we're going to see in the next  five years massive innovations in that  regard as well it is incredible to see a  sitting politician articulate bitcoin  bitcoin mining and its interfacing with  the energy grid in such a great way he  obviously understands the value of  bitcoin mining and he sees how bitcoin  is not simply a high consumer of  electricity but rather bitcoin can serve  as a great catalyst for growth  investment and build out of energy  infrastructure and so whether you're  looking at bitcoin as a financial asset  whether you're looking at as an  engineering feat or whether you are  looking at it as its positive impact on  the energy grid or other parts of our  non-bitcoin lives when you start to  understand is we are watching an asset  grow from the corners of the internet  into the mainstream to be repriced by  markets and to capture the imagination  of the entire world  that is what bitcoin is doing right  before us and people are looking and  saying hey it went up a little bit it  went down a little bit but they're  losing the bigger picture bitcoin has  now reached the mainstream and we are  likely to continue to see a drastic  increase in the adoption of the asset  not only from individual investors not  only from institutions like financial  institutions and corporations and not  only from nation states like el salvador  and maybe brazil and others but bitcoin  is also becoming an asset that is  penetrating every industry on earth  we're seeing the oil and gas the  capitalism of america start to embrace  this and i don't think it's going to  stop anytime soon
 

